{
  "$comment": "The language-neutral AGENT CASSETTES — the shared spine of journey testing (docs/journey-testing.md, axis 3). One canonical, frozen cassette per agentic RETURN STATE. Both ports (TS + Flutter) load THIS file, so a mock replay and the real transport emit identical frames and neither port can drift. The frame envelope (Sophia's SSE, services/sophia/sophia/streaming.py): progress | narrative_start | narrative | narrative_end | directive | done | error. A `directive` is either show_view {view_id, window_id, target: inline|panel, data, options} or notify {message, severity}. `branches` maps a view_event's event_type to the next cassette id — that's how a scripted, branching conversation stays deterministic. The event_type vocabulary is STANDARDIZED: always `submitted` or `cancelled`; the specifics ride in the payload (a confirmation sends {confirmed:true}, a selection sends the chosen ids, a form sends its values). Sophia's /event route only distinguishes cancelled vs submitted. Cassettes are recorded once from real Sophia then frozen; a contract test diffs frame SHAPES (not content) against the live agent so this can't rot.",
